Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Explain: composed explanations from reviewed phrases
 (304 prototype)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The model no longer writes the explanation. It picks, by id, one or two
"does" phrases and up to three "unsaid" items from a reviewed bank for the
engine-verified rule (data/explain-phrases.json, 43 moves); the server
writes the sentence:

  The words “<exact mark>” <does>[, and <does>]. The sentence does not say <a, b or c>.

- The mark is quoted exactly as the visitor wrote it, between curly
  quotes, or the reply is refused (E_OUT_PLAIN_TEXT): no clipping or
  stripping. The sentence's own straight scare quotes may stand inside
  as whole pairs; any other quotation mark, prime, sentence end,
  ellipsis, control, format or bidi character, or the product's name,
  refuses (checked raw and in NFKC form).
- Limits are unchanged and count the whole explanation, mark included
  (400 chars, 60 words, 3 sentences). pickLimits sizes each request's
  picks so every allowed choice fits; the prompt states the same
  numbers; a choice over them, or a mark too long for any, is E_OUT_HOW.
- Reply keys are exactly does,unsaid[,plainer]; unknown, other-rule,
  repeated or extra ids, extra keys and free text are refused.
- Plain-text, name, side and brand checks still run on the composed
  text as a backstop; the rewrite ("plainer") checks are unchanged.
- buildPrompt takes the engine-verified rule id (required) and lists
  that rule's options; it throws for a rule with no reviewed phrases.
- Free-text answers from earlier red teams (173 + 308) stay as
  regressions in both modes; the 28 round-3 composed attacks are
  regressions too.

Adoption is Brad's decision; this is a prototype for review. Call sites
(app.ts, eval/dry-run.ts) and canonical test helpers are described in a
separate note, not changed here.

